cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or code, please cite it as below."
title: "nl2sql-onprem-bench: an honest, reproducible benchmark of on-prem open-weight LLMs for Text-to-SQL on BIRD"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible harness and results for evaluating privately deployable
  open-weight LLMs on the BIRD dev split (n=1534, Execution Accuracy). Covers
  three model families across two generations under one matched protocol:
  Qwen2.5-Coder (7B/14B/32B) and CodeLlama-Instruct (7B/13B/34B) served on-prem
  with vLLM in fp16, and Llama-3.x (8B/70B) on a matched FP8 API serving. A
  model-agnostic recipe (schema linking, self-correction, self-consistency) is
  ablated component by component, with lexical and embedding schema linkers
  compared at matched gold-table recall, real wall-clock cost per stage, and
  every difference tested by the paired exact McNemar test. Reports the
  size x technique frontier, including negative results.
